body:
I've been scratching my head for the past hour because you're right, it does work today. So I figured that _somehow_ I managed to mix code from one project and results from another when filling the ticket.

But fortunately for me, It does happen with an Entity named `Company`, out of the `companies` table and `Companies` model. The class is empty, also PHP mem is 128M. 

`namespace App\Model\Entity;
 use Cake\ORM\Entity;
 class Company extends Entity {
}`

Sorry for getting you looking at the wrong thing...

Sure, the DB has only 2 rows, of 5 fields. 

```
//Controller/CompaniesController.php
namespace App\Controller;
use App\Controller\AppController;

class CompaniesController extends AppController {
    public function index() {
        $companies = $this->Companies->find('all');
        $this->set('companies', $companies);
    }
}

//Template/Companies/index.ctp
foreach ($companies as $company) {
    debug($company); //This one works
    // debug($company->$something); //This one causes the fatal error
}
```
